@page "/dashboard"
@inject AppState AppState

<PageTitle>Dashboard · BevTools</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <p class="bb-overline">Scenario · Rendering</p>
    <h1>Dashboard</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">
        A realistic component hierarchy: stat cards under a cascading value, a live clock, a user profile and the
        recent orders loaded over HTTP. It is where the component tree, the cause of every render and the most common
        avoidable cost in a Blazor app - renders driven only by a parent - are easiest to see.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> The dashboard</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        Plain application code, with one problem left in on purpose: tick <em>clock re-renders whole dashboard</em>
        and the clock's timer calls <code>StateHasChanged</code> on the whole page twice a second.
    </p>

    <div class="bb-demo">
        <div class="bb-demo-bar"><span class="bb-demo-label">Live</span><RendererStatus /></div>

        <CascadingValue Value="_settings">
            <div class="bb-toolbar">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="() => { _settings.Dense = !_settings.Dense; _settings.Version++; }">Toggle dense (cascading value → re-renders subscribers)</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="ChangeAccent">Change accent</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="AppState.Click">Click counter (AppState) = @AppState.Counters["clicks"]</button>
                <label class="bb-check"><input type="checkbox" @bind="_clockRerendersDashboard" /> clock re-renders whole dashboard (intentional problem)</label>
            </div>

            <div class="demo-tiles">
                <StatsCard Title="Revenue" Value="@_revenue.ToString("C0")" Trend="+4.2%" />
                <StatsCard Title="Orders" Value="@_orders.ToString()" Trend="+12" />
                <StatsCard Title="Visitors" Value="@_visitors.ToString("N0")" Trend="-1.8%" />
                <div class="demo-tile">
                    <h4 class="demo-tile-title">Server time</h4>
                    <LiveClock OnTick="OnClockTick" />
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="demo-tiles demo-tiles-pair">
                <UserProfile />
                <RecentOrders />
            </div>
        </CascadingValue>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> Components: the tree and the inspector</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        Open BevTools (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd><kbd>D</kbd>) on the <strong>Components</strong> tab.
        <code>Dashboard</code> sits under the site's layouts with its children: three <code>StatsCard</code>s,
        <code>LiveClock</code>, <code>UserProfile</code> and <code>RecentOrders</code>.
    </p>
    <ul class="bb-detail-list">
        <li>Select a <code>StatsCard</code>: its parameters (<code>Title</code>, <code>Value</code>, <code>Trend</code>), the cascading <code>DashboardSettings</code> it reads, and <em>Why did it render?</em> for every render it has had.</li>
        <li>Select <code>UserProfile</code>: its injected <code>UserSession</code> shows <code>AccessToken</code> and <code>Nickname</code> redacted - one by its name, the other by <code>[BevToolsSensitive]</code>.</li>
        <li>Press <em>Toggle dense</em> or <em>Change accent</em>: the cascading value changes and every card that reads it renders again.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> Profiler and Diagnostics: renders nobody asked for</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        Tick the checkbox, then open the <strong>Profiler</strong> and sort by renders: <code>Dashboard</code> and every
        card climb together. Selected in the inspector, the Revenue card says <em>Parent Dashboard re-rendered
        (parameters re-applied)</em> and marks those renders <em>forced</em>, because none of its parameter values
        changed - unlike the Visitors card, whose <code>Value</code> does. <strong>Diagnostics</strong> reports
        <em>Renders driven only by the parent</em> for each card.
    </p>
    <div class="bb-try">
        <a href="problems#problem-1" class="btn btn-outline">Problem 1, step by step →</a>
        <a href="products" class="btn btn-outline">A bigger cascade: Products →</a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> State, Network and Services</h3>
    <ul class="bb-detail-list">
        <li><strong>State</strong> → <code>AppState</code>: every press of <em>Click counter</em> is a named <code>Click</code> change, and every navigation a <code>Visit</code>. Its <code>ApiKey</code> is redacted.</li>
        <li><strong>Network</strong>: <code>GET /api/orders</code>, slow on purpose, and <code>GET /api/profile</code>, whose <code>Authorization</code> header is redacted.</li>
        <li><strong>Services</strong>: search <code>LeakyCache</code> and <code>ReportService</code> - a singleton capturing a scoped service and a circular dependency, registered in this app and never resolved.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    private readonly DashboardSettings _settings = new();
    private decimal _revenue = 128_430;
    private int _orders = 1_204;
    private int _visitors = 48_213;
    private bool _clockRerendersDashboard;

    private void ChangeAccent()
    {
        _settings.Accent = _settings.Accent == DashboardSettings.DefaultAccent ? DashboardSettings.AlternateAccent : DashboardSettings.DefaultAccent;
        _settings.Version++;
    }

    private void OnClockTick()
    {
        // Intentional problem #1: a timer in a child bubbles up and re-renders the entire dashboard twice a second.
        if (_clockRerendersDashboard)
        {
            _visitors++;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }
}
